xxt is an extremely small X11 terminal emulator. running memory usage recorded 1.6mb.

tldr:

	want a fully working terminal (colors, utf-8, alternate screen, scrollback)?
		patch main.c < patches/libvterm.patch
		cc -std=gnu89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -lvterm -O2

	want scrollback?
		patch main.c < patches/scrollback.patch
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	want vi mode?
		patch main.c < patches/vi-mode.patch
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	want scrollback and vi mode?
		patch main.c < patches/scrollback.patch
		patch main.c < patches/vi-mode.patch
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	want it as small as possible (194 lines, dumb terminal)?
		patch main.c < patches/bare.patch
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	none of the above?
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	then:
		install -m 755 xxt /usr/local/bin/xxt

	libvterm.patch cannot be combined with the other patches.

config:
	#define FONT "fixed" // default x11 font
	#define BG_COLOR "#000000" // black
	#define FG_COLOR "#ffffff" // white
	#define SCROLLBACK 10000 // lines kept (scrollback.patch; 2000 with libvterm.patch)

patches:
	to apply a patch:
		patch main.c < patches/<filename>

	to remove a patch:
		patch -R main.c < patches/<filename>

	if you apply several patches, remove them in reverse order.
	the patch must be removed from an otherwise unmodified main.c.
	after applying or removing a patch, recompile.
	patching adds lines, so the size numbers below only describe the unpatched xxt.

	patches/bare.patch
		strips xxt down to 194 lines. dumb terminal: TERM=dumb, escape
		sequences are ignored, no resize, no arrow keys, no window close handling.
		line editing in the shell still works. full-screen programs do not.
		conflicts with all other patches, use it alone. Only choose this if you are trying to run xxt on a toaster.

	patches/vi-mode.patch
		adds vi-style keyboard navigation, selection and copy/paste.
		no new dependencies. works on the visible screen only
		(with scrollback.patch it does not reach into the history).
		the current mode and search prompt are shown in the window title.

		modes:
			input	default. keys go to the shell.
			normal	cursor movement on the screen.
			visual	text selection (v = characters, V = lines).

		keys:
			Ctrl+Shift+Space	input -> normal
			i, q, Esc		normal -> input
			v, V			normal -> visual / visual-line (press again to cancel)
			Esc			visual -> normal

		normal and visual keys:
			h j k l, arrows		move
			w W b B e E		word motions
			0 ^ $			line start, first non-blank, line end
			gg G H M L		first line, last line, screen top / middle / bottom
			Ctrl-d Ctrl-u		half page down / up
			Ctrl-f Ctrl-b		page down / up
			f F t T ; ,		find character in line, repeat, reverse
			/ ? n N			search forward / backward, next, previous
			%			matching bracket
			counts			e.g. 5j, 3w, 10G
			o			visual: swap selection ends
			y, Enter		visual: yank selection and return to input
			yy, Y			normal: yank line(s)
			p			paste clipboard into the shell and return to input

		clipboard:
			yanked text is set as X PRIMARY and CLIPBOARD.
			Shift+Insert		paste PRIMARY (input mode)
			Ctrl+Shift+V		paste CLIPBOARD (input mode)

	patches/scrollback.patch
		adds a scrollback buffer (10000 lines, plain text, set with SCROLLBACK).
		no new dependencies.
		works with vi-mode.patch (apply in either order).

		keys:
			Shift+PageUp / Shift+PageDown	scroll half a screen
			Shift+Home / Shift+End		oldest line / back to the bottom
			mouse wheel			scroll 3 lines
			any other key			jump back to the bottom

		the top-right corner shows [offset/total] while scrolled.

	patches/libvterm.patch
		replaces the built-in escape parser with libvterm (0.3+).
		adds:
			16/256/truecolor
			bold, underline, strikethrough, reverse
			alternate screen
			cursor visibility
			UTF-8 (needs an iso10646-1 font)
			TERM=xterm-256color
			function keys, modifier keys, application cursor mode
		includes its own scrollback (2000 lines with colors, set with SCROLLBACK),
		same keys as scrollback.patch.
		conflicts with scrollback.patch and vi-mode.patch, do not combine.
		extra dependency: libvterm.
		libvterm.h uses inline, so strict -std=c89 does not work. use -std=gnu89.

compile:
	cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	with libvterm.patch:
		cc -std=gnu89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -lvterm -O2

install:
	install -m 755 xxt /usr/local/bin/xxt

deps:
	libX11. POSIX PTY functions come from libc on glibc.
	libvterm.patch also needs libvterm.

